{"title":"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Official_MAA)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Official MAA)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point chosen uniformly at random in the interior of the unit square with vertices at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232822edbaeb07a6a3b98beb9204331f701874e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0), (1,0), (1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The probability that the slope of the line determined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74b232026ee6094fef8ddd4d0caaee8300cfbff0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac58, \\frac38 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"57\" height=\"43\" /> is greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc960c165b21ba43f7a90caa2893d40409d6944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The areas bounded by the unit square and alternately bounded by the lines through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f307b55c914012f983cc8727038819e9212aff54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{5}{8},\\frac{3}{8}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"57\" height=\"43\" /> that are vertical or have a slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> show where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can be placed to satisfy the condition. One of the areas is a trapezoid with bases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b296e75784f6bd4fc2154d959b3d38ecc857728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855ce018e61e442b82913b94cf2fbf4775988b3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec32e2151ea26abffb5511d9aff292ccfb03276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />. The other area is a trapezoid with bases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/b/10b445b7deae82aa193344f9b4ceb7a42bfa44ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7/16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec32e2151ea26abffb5511d9aff292ccfb03276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855ce018e61e442b82913b94cf2fbf4775988b3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a4462215b3f5d9537b3bf6cf1c7aed20b86b183.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{3}{8}}{2}\\cdot\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{\\frac{7}{16}+\\frac{5}{8}}{2}\\cdot\\frac{3}{8}=\\frac{86}{256}=\\frac{43}{128}\\implies43+128=\\boxed{171}\\]\" width=\"472\" height=\"41\" />\n~mn28407\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Official_MAA.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Official_MAA)\">Solution 2 (Official MAA)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Official MAA)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The line through the fixed point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c75a5988e1eea448c341c321a483bc788980902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac58,\\frac38\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"57\" height=\"43\" /> with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc960c165b21ba43f7a90caa2893d40409d6944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> has equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f099a2a0467b601cac8fb7e7cfa1f08740363109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac12 x + \\frac1{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"37\" />. The slope between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the fixed point exceeds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc960c165b21ba43f7a90caa2893d40409d6944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> falls within the shaded region in the diagram below consisting of two trapezoids with area\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1dacf65fa2ac2d45dea84143eb934e3ee347cdd3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac1{16}+\\frac38}2\\cdot\\frac58 + \\frac{\\frac58+\\frac7{16}}2\\cdot\\frac38 = \\frac{43}{128}.\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"41\" />Because the entire square has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> the required probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/003d0bd711226db41cc1578c945cf9af51101c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{43}{128}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />. The requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/9213847eff58fb76c7895117d28a71f1ca4646e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$43+128 = 171$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/965b0d52cd7d196c2bcdbfbe72c01a25560ae5bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(8pt)); unitsize(4cm); pair A = (0,0);  pair B = (1,0);  pair C = (1,1);  pair D = (0,1);  pair F = (0, 1/16);  pair G = (1, 9/16);  pair H = (5/8, 0);  pair J = (5/8, 1);  pair K = IP(H--J, F--G);   pair P = (13/16, 12/16);  pair Q = extension(P,K,A,B);  pair R = extension(K,P,C,D);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);   label(&quot;$(0,0)$&quot;, A, SW);  label(&quot;$(1,0)$&quot;, B, SE);  label(&quot;$(1,1)$&quot;, C, E);  label(&quot;$(0,1)$&quot;, D, W);  filldraw(A--H--K--F--cycle, lightgray);  filldraw(K--G--C--J--cycle, lightgray);  dot(K);  dot(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, W);  draw(Q -- R, dashed);  label(&quot;$\\frac 38$&quot;, H--K, E); label(&quot;$\\frac 58$&quot;, K--J, W);  label(&quot;$\\frac 7{16}$&quot;, G--C, E);  label(&quot;$\\frac 38$&quot;, C--J, N);  label(&quot;$\\frac 1{16}$&quot;, A--F, dir(160));  [/asy]\" width=\"265\" height=\"232\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/x0QznvXcwHY?t=190\">https://youtu.be/x0QznvXcwHY?t=190</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VBwlVbM0GRw\">https://youtu.be/VBwlVbM0GRw</a> \n</p><p>~avn\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II\" title=\"2020 AIME II\">2020 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018011601\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 239/1000000\nPos